Package: plurx-player
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, mpv, python3 (>= 3.10), zenity
Recommends: desktop-file-utils, mesa-vulkan-drivers | vulkan-icd
Description: Cinema playback controls for plurx titles on Linux
 plurx Player plays titles handed over from the plurx web app in the system
 mpv, with Cinema controls, scoped server sessions and progress reporting.
 The package installs the Python launcher and Lua controls; mpv and its
 rendering libraries are supplied by the system mpv package.
 .
 HDR output needs a Wayland compositor with wp_color_manager_v1 in HDR mode,
 such as GNOME in HDR mode. An accurate target luminance needs a compositor
 that reports the panel's real luminance; stock compositors may report a
 default instead. Dolby Vision rendering and enhancement-layer composition
 require the native-dovi-api-1 compiled capability. Other builds negotiate
 server conversion to HDR10; this launcher does not supply renderer support.
